<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Plain-language draft terms for using the DataDecision website and public research material."
  path="/terms/"
  updated="24 Aug 2026"
>
  <h2>Website information, not professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    The website explains DataDecision’s current methods and services. Public articles and templates
    are general information, not legal, financial or guaranteed business advice. A consultancy
    engagement begins only under a separate written agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>No outcome guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    AI-search visibility is sampled and changes with engines, prompts, sessions, locations and time.
    DataDecision does not guarantee placement, citation, rankings, traffic, leads, pipeline or
    revenue on any search or AI surface.
  </p>

  <h2>Public methods and templates</h2>
  <p>
    You may use the public templates for internal evaluation. Do not remove required evidence fields
    when presenting a resulting measurement as if it followed the published method. Keep dates,
    samples, baselines, method versions and limitations attached to public citations.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Technical guidance is dated because provider policies and product behavior change. DataDecision
    aims to correct material errors, but does not promise that every public note remains current
    after its stated update date.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not misuse the site, interfere with its operation, submit unlawful material, impersonate
    another person or use the public contact path to send spam or malicious content.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Articles link to provider documentation and other public sources. Those services control their
    own content, availability and terms. A link is evidence or context, not an endorsement or
    partnership claim.
  </p>

  <h2>Commercial terms</h2>
  <p>
    Scope, fees, taxes, credit terms, confidentiality, intellectual property, payment timing,
    cancellation and liability must be stated in the signed engagement agreement. This website does
    not silently add commercial terms that are absent from that agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing terms and contact</h2>
  <p>
    The legal entity, jurisdiction, notice address and dispute process require founder/legal
    confirmation before publication. They are intentionally not guessed in this draft.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
